{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5297) from a work queue in the go-unix-utils project. The task is to implement srd029-comm requirements R2.1 through R2.4 — the column suppression flags (-1, -2, -3) for the `cmd/comm` utility. The existing implementation already handles R1.x (basic three-column comparison). The task requires:\n   - Modifying `cmd/comm/main.go` to add -1, -2, -3 flag parsing and column suppression with correct indentation adjustment\n   - Adding differential test cases to `cmd/comm/comm_test.go` covering R2.1-R2.4\n   - All tests must pass (or skip gracefully if gcomm is not installed)\n   - Existing R1.x functionality must not break\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU comm utility: compares two sorted files line by line, producing three-column output\n   - Column suppression: -1 suppresses col1 (unique to file1), -2 suppresses col2 (unique to file2), -3 suppresses common lines\n   - Indentation adjustment (R2.4): when columns are suppressed, remaining columns shift left so the leftmost visible column has no leading tab\n   - Differential testing via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` against `gcomm` (Homebrew GNU reference binary)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - LC_ALL=C byte-for-byte comparison (no locale collation)\n   - Go build: `go build -o bin/comm ./cmd/comm/`; test: `go test ./cmd/comm/ -count=1`\n   - Execution constitution rules: no git commands, 40-line function limit, copyright headers, write-first strategy\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd029-comm.yaml`\n     - Full SRD for comm. R2 section specifies column suppression flags:\n       - R2.1: -1 suppresses column 1, remaining columns shift left\n       - R2.2: -2 suppresses column 2, remaining columns shift left\n       - R2.3: -3 suppresses column 3, combining all three produces no output\n       - R2.4: Tab indentation adjusts so leftmost output column has no leading tab\n\n   - `cmd/comm/main.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Current implementation handles R1.x only (basic three-column output)\n     - No flag parsing exists — `main()` expects exactly 2 args\n     - Key functions: `main()`, `run()`, `openInput()`, `compare()`, `drain()`, `writeLine()`, `epipeOr1()`\n     - `writeLine(w, col, line)` uses hardcoded tabs: col1=\"\", col2=\"\\t\", col3=\"\\t\\t\"\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     package main\n     import (\n         \"bufio\"\n         \"errors\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"io\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"syscall\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         w := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n         args := os.Args[1:]\n         if len(args) != 2 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"comm: missing operand\\n\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         exitCode := run(w, args[0], args[1])\n         if err := w.Flush(); err != nil {\n             if errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE) { os.Exit(0) }\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         os.Exit(exitCode)\n     }\n     func run(w *bufio.Writer, path1, path2 string) int { /* opens files, calls compare */ }\n     func openInput(name string) (io.Reader, io.Closer, error) { /* handles \"-\" for stdin */ }\n     func compare(w *bufio.Writer, r1, r2 io.Reader) int { /* main comparison loop */ }\n     func drain(w *bufio.Writer, s1, s2 *bufio.Scanner, have1, have2 bool) int { /* drains remaining lines */ }\n     func writeLine(w *bufio.Writer, col int, line string) error { /* writes with tab indent based on col 1/2/3 */ 